  "body": "`inputmode` spec says,\r\n> User agents can support the inputmode attribute on form controls (such as the value of textarea elements), or in elements in an editing host (e.g., using contenteditable).\r\n\r\nWhen I test `inputmode` attribute for Blink (Chrome/Android 82) and WebKit (iOS 13.3.1) implementation. Both implementers use it for editing host only.\r\n\r\nExample, The following HTML doesn't work to number input on Chrome/Android and iOS Safari\r\n```\r\n<div contenteditable><div inputmode=numeric>12345</div></div>\r\n```\r\nAlso, of course, this works.\r\n```\r\n<div contenteditable inputmode=numeric><div>12345</div></div>\r\n```\r\n\r\nSo I would like to request that user agents can support the inputmode attribute on **editing host** for contenteditable, not \"in elements in an editing host\".",
